WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.959
- Back in the day, 

00:00:00.959 --> 00:00:03.503
when I picked up the game of football, 

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.255
AND1 mixtapes was big.

00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:08.591
One day I was out at practice, and we was kinda just doing different moves. 

00:00:08.591 --> 00:00:11.052
I said, “You know what? I’mma start spinning, I’mma start drop step.

00:00:11.052 --> 00:00:13.555
I’mma do this type of thing in football, see if it works.”

00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:15.724
Sure enough, I was making people miss. 

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:21.813
♪♪♪ 

00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:25.775
- Dwight Freeney, what’s good with you?
- Hey, I would give you 

00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:26.651
the dap, but, you know.

00:00:26.651 --> 00:00:28.361
- Hey, It’s different times now. It’s different times now. 
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.362
- How you livin’ during ‘rona, man?

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:29.863
- How you livin’ during ‘rona, man?

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:32.323
- Right now I’m retired, so it’s easy. 

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:33.825
You know what I’m saying?  I’m not doing much.

00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:35.035
It’s definitely insane.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.372
- You are a legend upstate.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:42.792
You played at Syracuse. I grew up in Texas,
so I was Big 12 Country, OK? 

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:44.878
I didn’t watch too much Big East football. 
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:45.336 --> 00:00:46.963
- But when Vick was on, people was watching.

00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:47.589
- Yeah.

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:50.008
- Do you have a memorable story at all

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:53.803
during your time playing against Vick, Virginia Tech-‘Cuse, Big East Football?

00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:55.138
- Oh, absolutely. 

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:57.974
I mean, Mike Vick, we laugh about it now. 

00:00:57.974 --> 00:01:00.226
My junior year when we played him 

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:06.775
in the Carrier Dome, it happened to be my best individual game of my entire career.

00:01:06.775 --> 00:01:08.401
- High school, college, pro—best game?

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.278
- Best game ever.  

00:01:10.278 --> 00:01:12.113
I don’t know what came over me, man.

00:01:12.113 --> 00:01:15.658
It got to a point where the ball would snap in slow motion. 

00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:20.288
You know, I would already be moving, and the ball is moving, 
and that offensive tackle is still in his stance. 

00:01:20.288 --> 00:01:22.957
He can’t even move. I’m, like, three steps past him.

00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:25.710
Mike ain’t have a chance that game, man. 

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:26.836
- How crazy was it? 

00:01:26.836 --> 00:01:28.713
What numbers did you put up in that game that made it so crazy?

00:01:28.713 --> 00:01:30.715
- Dude, I had 4.5 sacks.

00:01:30.715 --> 00:01:33.426
Coulda probably had six sacks that game. 

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.428
I was on a whole ‘nother planet that game.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:40.308
But in the end, that game was probably my most memorable game 

00:01:40.308 --> 00:01:43.228
for, one reason, having a great game, 

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:47.357
but the second reason is I ended up getting hurt in that game.

00:01:47.357 --> 00:01:48.108
- You got hurt?

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.527
- I got hurt hitting him.

00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:51.277
- What happened?

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:54.447
- He ducked one particular play. 

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:58.409
His helmet hit me right here in my abdomen. 

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:03.873
I ended up having a lacerated spleen from that situation. 

00:02:03.873 --> 00:02:06.835
So I get hurt by hitting a quarterback.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.421
- Supposed to be the other way around.
- So, yeah ,exactly. 

00:02:10.421 --> 00:02:14.759
So now, you know, that builds up my hatred for quarterbacks even more. 
You know what I’m saying? 

00:02:14.759 --> 00:02:18.179
I can’t hit y'all, y'all hurtin’ me. So nah, nah, I can’t have that.

00:02:18.179 --> 00:02:20.807
- You played with a lacerated spleen? Did you know that during the game?

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:25.562
- No, listen. I played the rest of the game, didn’t know I had a lacerated spleen. 

00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:30.441
We played on Saturdays. On Monday, I woke up. Everything was in slow motion. 

00:02:30.441 --> 00:02:33.486
My eyes was blurry. I couldn’t even function. 

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:36.281
Skin was popping. All types of stuff was happening to me.

00:02:36.281 --> 00:02:39.075
The trainers, they didn’t know what was wrong with me. 

00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:42.912
So they had to quarantine me. I was like the first guy to get quarantined.

00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:44.747
- You were ahead of your time!
- We goin’ full-circle now. 

00:02:44.747 --> 00:02:46.875
They did all types of different studies on me. 

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:50.253
And they found out through CAT scans that I was bleeding internally. 

00:02:50.253 --> 00:02:52.672
They started giving me antibiotics.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.841
I ended up being allergic to the penicillin. 

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:59.053
So now all of a sudden, I got this lacerated spleen, I’m taking medicine I’m allergic to, 

00:02:59.053 --> 00:03:01.306
my skin is breaking out, all types of crazy stuff—

00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:02.682
- You’re bleeding internally

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.225
- Bleeding internally just from hitting a quarterback.

00:03:04.225 --> 00:03:05.393
- [Laughing]  

00:03:05.393 --> 00:03:07.020
- Right? It’s crazy!

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.938
- So how did it all get resolved? 

00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:11.524
I mean, you said you’re dealing with this for a couple of weeks. You still playing?

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.776
- Well, I’m on wrap for the rest of the year. I’m done. 

00:03:13.776 --> 00:03:14.986
I’m done, done, done. 

00:03:14.986 --> 00:03:18.031
I ended up losing 30, 40 pounds that junior year

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.115
- 30, 40 pounds?!  

00:03:19.115 --> 00:03:21.618
- It was crazy, man. I looked, I looked sick. 

00:03:21.618 --> 00:03:25.622
I was, like, 250-something to, like, 215.

00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:26.915
I thought I was on my way out.

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:27.874
- You thought your career was done?

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:28.291
- Done!

00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:30.335
The rest of the year I was done. 

00:03:30.335 --> 00:03:33.213
Ended up coming back in spring football, got my weight back up 

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.047
and that was it. 

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.590
- How the hell you put back 40 pounds?

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:36.925
- Man, I started eating. 

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:37.884
- [Laughing]

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.094
- I started eating. I’m Jamaican, so—

00:03:40.094 --> 00:03:41.387
- A lotta jerk and oxtail?

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.389
- Yeah, a lotta oxtail, a lotta curried goat, 

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.516
you know what I’m saying? That’s what I was on.

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:47.435
- That’s crazy to think that 

00:03:47.435 --> 00:03:50.063
your career could have ended before it even started professionally.  

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.689
How do you block that out? 

00:03:51.689 --> 00:03:53.233
I mean, your whole job is to hit the quarterback, 

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.777
so every single time you’re rushing the quarterback, is that on your mind?   

00:03:55.777 --> 00:03:58.321
- Well, I have a hatred for quarterbacks.

00:03:58.321 --> 00:03:59.697
- [Laughing]

00:03:59.697 --> 00:04:03.117
- And you’re supposed to have a hatred for quarterbacks 
if you’re a guy who’s going after ‘em. 

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:08.706
- When the Jets was in the AFC Championship, 2009-2010, they ended up playing us. 

00:04:08.706 --> 00:04:10.583
This is when these rules started coming out, 

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.586
which destroyed me, which even gave me more fuel to hate ‘em. 

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:14.420
It’s a strike zone. 

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.839
Fourth quarter, we up two scores.

00:04:16.839 --> 00:04:19.676
I’m going out, burning around the corner. 

00:04:19.676 --> 00:04:21.135
It’s a screen pass. 

00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:24.764
I got Sanchez lined up to completely just wipe him out.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.766
- I can’t imagine what was going on in your mind.
- Something goes through my head 

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.894
saying, “You know what? Don’t hit the quarterback.

00:04:29.894 --> 00:04:32.897
It’s close. You might get a penalty. 

00:04:32.897 --> 00:04:38.403
You might hurt the guy. I jump over him, do a little turn just so I don’t hit him.

00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:39.404
- You avoided the quarterback? 

00:04:39.404 --> 00:04:39.904
- I avoided him. 

00:04:39.904 --> 00:04:43.741
When I land, he rolls on my ankle.

00:04:43.741 --> 00:04:50.081
Completely severs the ligaments in my ankle.  I have a third-degree high ankle sprain

00:04:50.081 --> 00:04:54.961
just because I’m trying to avoid hitting a quarterback. 

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.838
Now I’m supposed to be out four to six weeks. 

00:04:56.838 --> 00:04:58.298
The Super Bowl was in two weeks. 

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.466
We probably lost the Super Bowl cuz I was hurt. 

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.510
Never again am I gonna avoid a quarterback.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:05.263
If I see one right now, I might give him a little—

00:05:05.263 --> 00:05:07.056
- We ain’t got no quarterbacks on set, do we? 

00:05:07.056 --> 00:05:08.766
We ain’t got no high school quarterbacks?
- Yeah, exactly!

00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:11.019
- No peewee quarterbacks? No?  We good?
- If you played, you might get hit

00:05:11.019 --> 00:05:11.686
We good?
Seriously.

00:05:11.686 --> 00:05:12.729
All right, cool. 

00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:14.230
So when you think of Mark Sanchez’s name now—

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:15.648
- Don’t let me see Mark Sanchez, 

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:16.524
- [Laughing]

00:05:16.524 --> 00:05:17.108
OK?

00:05:17.108 --> 00:05:20.111
- “Remember that time I avoided you and had that high ankle sprain?” 

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:22.322
I’mma give him a little forearm shiver. 

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.073
Something. Something. 

00:05:24.073 --> 00:05:26.659
We ended up losing that Super Bowl, and I’m still upset about that.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.244
- Was that the Saints?

00:05:28.244 --> 00:05:30.455
- Yeah, to the Saints. 

00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:31.998
I don’t like talking about that.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:32.790
- Say less.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.208
- [Laughing]

